@startuml state-incident
!include _style.iuml
title State machine — Incident (services/incidents.py TRANSITIONS)

[*] --> Open

state Open {
  [*] --> SUBMITTED
  SUBMITTED --> VERIFIED : verify(priority, rationale)\n/ notify reporter
  SUBMITTED --> REJECTED : reject(rationale)
  SUBMITTED --> NEEDS_INFORMATION : requestInformation(question)\n/ notify reporter
  NEEDS_INFORMATION --> NEEDS_INFORMATION : requestInformation(question)
  NEEDS_INFORMATION --> SUBMITTED : citizenReply(text, location?)
  NEEDS_INFORMATION --> VERIFIED : verify(priority, rationale)
  NEEDS_INFORMATION --> REJECTED : reject(rationale)
  VERIFIED --> DISPATCHED : dispatchCreated
  VERIFIED --> RESOLVED : resolve(rationale)
  DISPATCHED --> RESOLVED : resolve(rationale)
}

Open --> CLOSED : close(reason)\n[CLOSURE permission and\n(no open dispatch or override)]
CLOSED --> Open[H] : reopen(reason)\n[CLOSURE permission]

note right of Open
  Every transition: optimistic version check,
  incident_status_history row, audit_logs row.
  Invariant: VERIFIED, DISPATCHED and RESOLVED
  require verified_priority (database CHECK).
end note
note bottom of CLOSED
  Not a final state: reopen returns through the shallow
  history state H to the state the incident was closed
  from, except RESOLVED → VERIFIED, REJECTED → SUBMITTED,
  and SUBMITTED when no priority was ever set.
end note
@enduml
